  The reel_script and slides say the complaint was filed 'today' / 'இன்று' with a date of November 14, which matches the article; no issue there. However, the reel_script and slides present the complaint's allegations as facts without the attribution, and the article only states what the complaint says — the reel_script attributes the claims to the complaint correctly, but the tamil_headline states 'அவதூறு' (defamation) as established fact, which the article does not establish; the article only reports a complaint alleging defamation.
  The slides_spec 'hl1' says 'ஆத்தூரில் வன்னியர் சமூகத்தை அவதூறு' as a stated fact and the caption header calls it 'அவதூறு செய்ததாக', which is acceptable, but the reel_script's first sentence says 'அவதூறு செய்ததாக' while the complaint's wording is about 'அவதூறு' remarks — minor framing issue only.
  The slides_spec line 'ஜீவசகாப்தன் மீது நடவடிக்கை' (hl2) reads as if action has been taken against him, whereas the article says the complainants demand action; this misstates the status of the matter.
